Dear Alex,

Commercial terms for your response:

- Fixed price for implementation. The approved budget is GBP 1.1 million including the
  first year of support; anything above that goes back to the Trust board.
- The patient portal must be live by 1 February 2027, before the new financial year
  targets for DNA reduction start. Referrals can follow by June 2027.
- Availability: 99.9%, 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, with service credits of 5% of the
  monthly charge per 0.1% below target.
- Patient numbers for sizing: plan for 600,000 registered patients by 2028 (new housing
  developments in the catchment).
- Milestone payments: 20% at design sign-off, 40% at portal go-live, 30% at referral
  go-live, 10% after 90 days of stable running.
- Delay damages of GBP 5,000 per working day if portal go-live slips for reasons within
  the supplier's control.
- Please show each allowance for unknowns separately, with its hours, rather than
  spreading it across rates. The board wants to see what we are paying for uncertainty.
- Support: 1-hour response for priority 1 incidents, 24/7.

Kind regards,
Priya Natarajan
